.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:17:00-07:00","id":862980,"title":"","content":"I've only ever played one Sid, a Greensid Disco Ninja, and I didn't create enough/find enough opportunity to make great use of Astrology or my weirder Charms to really get the strangeness across, but I had fun once I started getting the point of them, and learned to play with preparation. <br /> <br /> It was kinda hard, coming off playing a Lunar that reacted to everything rather than needing to be proactive, but it was fun. I'd do it again. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:19:07-07:00","id":862981,"title":"","content":"I currently play two Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Single Step Serafina - an Independent Chosen of Journeys from the near East who promotes communcation between the various departments and factions of Sidereals she's a master of Swaying Grass Dance Style and wears the Thousand League Boots for righteous asskicking.<br /> Autumn Shade- A Chosen of Endings record keeper and biographer in the early First Age, she was one of the first students of Single Point Style and wields the Reaper Daiklave Silent Quill a blade that's virtually invisible in motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:23:39-07:00","id":862982,"title":"","content":"Our Skype game just switched to Sidereals. I'm playing a Chosen of Serenity named Anuli. She is a Righteous Devil Martial Artist dual wielding twin Star Metal Plasma Repeaters called &quot;the Peacemakers&quot;. <br /> <br /> Yes, I based the entire character concept off of a bad pun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:51:09-07:00","id":862988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=862982#post862982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our Skype game just switched to Sidereals. I'm playing a Chosen of Serenity named Anuli. She is a Righteous Devil Martial Artist dual wielding twin Star Metal Plasma Repeaters called &quot;the Peacemakers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yes, I based the entire character concept off of a bad pun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like Iron Siaka. She finds serenity in finding the enemies of Creation and smashing in their skulls.<br /> <br /> Alas, while I have a Full Circle of Sidereal buddies... Well, four of them have appropriate or thematic Martial Arts in the corebook. The Chosen of Journeys, alas, her associated Martial Art wasn't in the book.<br /> <br /> <i>Why</i> couldn't one of the backers have picked Crystal Chameleon style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:59:02-07:00","id":862990,"title":"","content":"I know, right? My Greensid loved that style. So loud, so flashy, yet so very effective at hiding you! <br /> <br /> Although I could be just as happy using Ebon Shadow tho. The new version is really nice, despite my various misgivings about Ex3. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/748-ultrafennec","name":"UltraFennec","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar748_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:06:47-07:00","id":862992,"title":"","content":"My first sidereal was a chosen of battles with a group of 3 solars...<br /> <br /> The eclipse decided when the unconquered sun wouldn't meet him in his first trip to heaven, to declare war on heaven and since he had just taken over Gem, make the cult of the Sniveling Ratman the official religion. <br /> <br /> he through getting very drunk and not listening to me wound up with a backlog of 17 eclipse oath botches stocked on himself by the time that game ended.....<br /> <br /> my character went from cheerful gold faction to wondering whats the best way to say &quot;you were right&quot; to kejack without sounding like you were desperate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:10:43-07:00","id":862995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=862992#post862992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first sidereal was a chosen of battles with a group of 3 solars...<br /> <br /> The eclipse decided when the unconquered sun wouldn't meet him in his first trip to heaven, to declare war on heaven and since he had just taken over Gem, make the cult of the Sniveling Ratman the official religion.<br /> <br /> he through getting very drunk and not listening to me wound up with a backlog of 17 eclipse oath botches stocked on himself by the time that game ended.....<br /> <br /> my character went from cheerful gold faction to wondering whats the best way to say &quot;you were right&quot; to kejack without sounding like you were desperate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering how most Solar games go, I imagine Chejop Kejak's plan for the Gold Faction is &quot;Let them actually interact with Solars and see if they still support the vision of Gold&quot;<br /> <br /> /Let's not turn this thread into a Gold/Bronze Vision Flame War, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:23:04-07:00","id":862999,"title":"","content":"I'm very excited for them now that the TN shenanigans are just part of the excellency now. I loved sidereals but hated building them because of all the &quot;you need to do this to start to get things out of the system&quot; with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:45:18-07:00","id":863008,"title":"","content":"I really want to like Sidereals. If 3e continues to deliver on presentation and mechanics the way it has so far, I think I really will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:06:57-07:00","id":863017,"title":"","content":"I hope the new ones are easier for players to integrate into a non-Sid group. Seems there is always one player that wants to play a Sidereal in a Solar group. <br /> Mind you, given how far down the line that splat is... *sigh*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:15:55-07:00","id":863019,"title":"","content":"Sadly, I've only ever ben able to play one Sidereal. He was a Chosen of Endings who worked for the Bureau of Destiny as a sort of &quot;designated rival&quot; to mortal heroes chosen by the Bureau for a specific purpose. The guy who would always be one step ahead of the NPC hero and serve as a motivator for the chosen one. He cruised around on a magically conjured chariot with a quartet of Dragon-Blooded ladies who fawned over him as apart of the act to anger the chosen one and spur him on to his destiny.<br /> <br /> He was basically Gary Oak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:27:32-07:00","id":863026,"title":"","content":"I have in my mind a kid sidereal (kid being a relative term, looks like a kid, probably a bit older now) who is a chosen of endings that actually likes her job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:52:11-07:00","id":863064,"title":"","content":"Yup. Not going to lie, Sidereals are a big reason I'm even still here, despite so much of Exalted grinding my gears (the other primary reason being Alchemicals). They're just such an unique player experience, that you don't really get in many other games easily. I can get what Solars offer better by playing M&amp;M, but I can't get a proper Sidereal experience as easily in other games. <br /> <br /> Fate-powered Men In Black Ninjas with poetic powers and heavenly bureaucracy is rather an unique thing, and I really enjoy that feel they have of being a part of something, beholden to more than themselves and their whims. I've said at times that a Sidereal's greatest power are not their charms, but their Background dots. And that's a feel I enjoy. <br /> <br /> So basiclaly, yeah, Sidereal fans represent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T01:45:22-07:00","id":863076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=863064#post863064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate-powered Men In Black Ninjas with poetic powers and heavenly bureaucracy is rather an unique thing, and I really enjoy that feel they have of being a part of something, beholden to more than themselves and their whims. I've said at times that a Sidereal's greatest power are not their charms, but their Background dots. And that's a feel I enjoy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now reminded of when I remade my five Sidereals for Exalted Modern. They wore slick FBI suits and played the &quot;MIB of Heaven&quot; angle to a T, working to support Solar Resistance against Infernal rule.<br /> <br /> I never actually USED them in any games, but it did make me imagine my Chosen of Serenity riding a boss motorcycle, using shortcuts through Fate, while my Chosen of Battles rides behind her taking potshots at an opponent, using Sidereal Magic Bullets to take out all their tires at once.<br /> <br /> My brain goes strange places on occasion, but it's usually worth the trip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T02:12:37-07:00","id":863083,"title":"","content":"Wait, no flame wars? What happens when the Sun loving goldies and the fun loving bronzies start having it out? Oh wait, they don't because in one of my favourite comics of second edition they give eachother some friendly ribbing and then get to work and have a blast doing it. I credit that comic for showing half the reasons playing a Sidereal is fun as hell! Galavanting around creation on dragonback, stomping out corruption, and if you did you job right nobody even knew you were there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T05:35:49-07:00","id":863118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=862971#post862971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we come after Dragonblooded, Exigents, and Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect that the order is going to be 'Original, New to 3e and related to Original' for upcoming releases. Plus, Abyssals have generally come out before Sidereals before.<br /> <br /> So, 'Dragonblooded / Exigents' - 'Lunars / Blankity Blanks' - 'Abyssals / Liminals' - 'Sidereals / Getiman'<br /> <br /> Assuming a two fat splat release a year, that's around four years for our precious cinnamon bun fate ninjas.<br /> And now I made myself sad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T05:39:17-07:00","id":863119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=863118#post863118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now I made myself sad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know... I know... Here have some wine. It will make you feel better. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T05:54:49-07:00","id":863124,"title":"","content":"I've only played one Sidereal, in a Heaven's Reach game no less -- a Chosen of Serenity who was a princess of a small kingdom of planets who was basically stuck training with a desk job and weird shit started happening all over the galaxy. When she could wait no longer, she ran away from home and joined a band of rogues to set thing right.<br /> <br /> This was the character I designed to be as much a disney princess as I possibly could. She was lovely, could sing and did so often, even in combat, could speak with animals, etc.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I always enjoyed Sidereal Charms. Their trees are set up in interesting ways, with weird but interesting themes. I've written a lot of custom Sidereal Charms over the years. Linguistics Charm from Always Coming Home which let you seem like and be treated as a native of wherever you're at to Righteous Verse of the Ages which lets you grapple people with poetry. I reused the 1e Charm name Hot-Eyed Snake Whisper as a Socialize Charm that lets you if someone desires you, and how. An Investigation Charm Origin of Knowledge, letting you how a source got its information; the ultimate citation power.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to seeing what Ex3 Sidereals comes out with. If Solars were any indication, they're gonna have a lot more Charms, and a lot more ways to hang interesting effects onto Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T07:32:57-07:00","id":863144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Limited Reagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=863124#post863124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always enjoyed Sidereal Charms. Their trees are set up in interesting ways, with weird but interesting themes. I've written a lot of custom Sidereal Charms over the years. Linguistics Charm from <b>Always Coming Home</b> which let you seem like and be treated as a native of wherever you're at to <b>Righteous Verse of the Ages</b> which lets you grapple people with poetry. I reused the 1e Charm name Hot-Eyed Snake Whisper as a <b>Socialize Charm that lets you if someone desires you, and how</b>. An Investigation Charm <b>Origin of Knowledge</b>, letting you how a source got its information; the ultimate citation power.</div> </div> </div> </div>*steals*<br /> <br /> (I mean, I've already used Hot-Eyed Snake Whisper as a name, so I'll have to make something else up for that effect, but still)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T08:54:04-07:00","id":863173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=863083#post863083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, no flame wars? What happens when the Sun loving goldies and the fun loving bronzies start having it out? Oh wait, they don't because in one of my favourite comics of second edition they give eachother some friendly ribbing and then get to work and have a blast doing it. I credit that comic for showing half the reasons playing a Sidereal is fun as hell! Galavanting around creation on dragonback, stomping out corruption, and if you did you job right nobody even knew you were there.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS<br /> <br /> in that game mentioned above, one of my character's best friends in the Five Score Fellowship was Bronze. They even were made to work against eachother at times, and a couple times he lost, a couple times my battle lost. they never fought openly. The end of each story involving them was like the end of boston legal. Sitting on a balcony in a manse in heaven just having classy drinks and talking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:51:07-07:00","id":863841,"title":"","content":"I've always loved the Sidereals...awesome thematic structure built up around them. I've always preferred that comic's presentation of how the opposing factions generally relate to one another as opposed to the active hatred that some of the other books put on them. Sure, I could see some of the Elder Siddies who were alive during the Usurpation having very, very strong feelings on the matter...but most of the rest of them, not so much.<br /> <br /> I'm actually working on a story about a Sidereal...though it's a rather non-typical one. It's the story of Amara, Chosen of the Maiden of Secrets, Chair (and only active member) of the Convention on the Multiverse.<br /> <br /> She's not really active around Creation, because she isn't there much...she isn't a member of any faction for the same reason, but has the ear of pretty much all the elder Sidereals. This is mostly because she brings very interesting stuff back from other worlds and her 'debriefings' tend to turn into a social event based around enjoying whatever 'alien delicacies' she brought them this time (Chejop is partial to those 2-piece black cookies with a cream filling)...and, naturally, she and Chejop (her nominal superior) are the only two with invitation rights to these &quot;official debriefings.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:57:07-07:00","id":863848,"title":"","content":"I've never had the pleasure of playing a Sidereal, but I've GMed for a few PCs. In our Heaven's Reach shard game, we had a Chosen of Secrets who was sort of... counter-intuitive. He was given no instruction on how to use his powers when he exalted, and he was an anti-government anarchist who believed ALL information should be freely available. So he didn't <i>keep</i> secrets, so much as <i>find out and reveal</i> secrets. If he were a 3rd ed character, he would have a Defining Intimacy of &quot;Nothing should be secret&quot; as that's how he acted. It was a fun twist on the paradigm and both the player and myself really enjoyed it in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:00:57-07:00","id":863849,"title":"","content":"Chejop Kejak is a great character to put in to crazy situations or give strange quirks to. <br /> <br /> In my quest, Elder Kejak pissed off another Elder Sidereal. Magna exist in the quest's setting, so this Elder used his influence to create a character based on Kejak in one of the manga. This Manga being &quot;Pretty Dragon Princess Meru&quot; and the new character &quot;Uncle Jack&quot;, who is a Panty Thief. Kejak was not amused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:15:30-07:00","id":863860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=863849#post863849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chejop Kejak is a great character to put in to crazy situations or give strange quirks to.<br /> <br /> In my quest, Elder Kejak pissed off another Elder Sidereal. Magna exist in the quest's setting, so this Elder used his influence to create a character based on Kejak in one of the manga. This Manga being &quot;Pretty Dragon Princess Meru&quot; and the new character &quot;Uncle Jack&quot;, who is a Panty Thief. Kejak was not amused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elaborate-but-petty revenge is the BEST revenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:19:35-07:00","id":863865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862940-maiden-approved-fun-the-sidereal-fan-club-thread?p=863860#post863860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Elaborate-but-petty revenge is the BEST revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Svante, the main character of the quest, arranged for a goat to be placed in Kejak's office. <br /> <br /> Kejak is not having a good day (still the same day in the quest).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}